This code provides a thread-safe implementation of a dynamic list managing `Entry` structures, with mechanisms for initialization, resizing buffers, adding entries, retrieving, and updating entries. It uses mutexes to ensure safe concurrent access while minimizing lock contention by protecting only necessary sections of the code. The logging function handles allocation failures, aiding in monitoring memory management issues.']

