### Integration via PHP FFI

To call the C function from PHP using FFI, ensure that your PHP environment supports FFI and that the shared library is available.

#### Example for PHP FFI (assuming a compiled shared library `librandom.so`)

```php
<?php
$ffi = FFI::cdef("
    void initialize_random(int range_min, int range_max);
    long* allocate_long_array(size_t size);
    int* allocate_int_array(size_t size);
    record* allocate_record_array(size_t size);
    void populate_records(record *records, size_t num_records, int range_min, int range_max);
    void free_memory(long *long_array, int *int_array, record *record_array);

    typedef struct {
        int value;
    } record;
", "path/to/librandom.so");

$ffi->initialize_random(1, 100);
$numRecords = 10;

// Allocate memory for records
$records = $ffi->allocate_record_array($numRecords);

try {
    $ffi->populate_records($records, $numRecords, 1, 100);

    // Use the populated records as needed

} catch (FFI\Exception $e) {
    echo "Error: ", $e->getMessage();
}

// Free allocated memory
$ffi->free_memory(null, null, $records);
?>
